The first-party source is distributed under Apache-2.0, except files that
identify another license. Solidity source files carry MIT identifiers.

The proof backend is pinned to Plonky3 revision
0d803737b681774186cd283b1fd2d8e493655c82.
https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3

The vendor directory retains the original Apache-2.0 and MIT licenses of
p3-air, p3-uni-stark, p3-fri and p3-keccak. The local copies adapt transcript
binding, transition stride, hiding-capacity checks, compiled verification,
streaming checkpoints and SBF execution.
The talc allocator retains its own license and SBF integration changes.

Public experiment artifacts include transaction receipts, signed wires,
public proofs and testnet program bytes. Local fixtures use documented
public research seeds. Private research roots and network credentials are
stored separately.
